[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Did You Want to Tell Me Something?]
[00:15.01]Why did the writer become very worried?
[00:21.27]Dentists always ask questions when it is impossible for you to answer.
[00:27.87]My dentist had just pulled out one of my teeth and had told me to rest for a while.
[00:34.58]I tried to say something,
[00:36.60]but my mouth was full of cotton wool.
[00:40.91]He knew I collected match boxes and asked me whether my collection was growing.
[00:48.27]He then asked me how my brother was and whether I liked my new job in London.
[00:54.93]In answer to these questions I either nodded or made strange noises.
[01:01.35]Meanwhile, my tongue was busy searching out the hole where the tooth had been.
[01:08.71]I suddenly felt very worried, but could not say anything.
[01:13.61]When the dentist at last removed the cotton wool from my mouth,
[01:18.79]I was able to tell him that he had pulled out the wrong tooth.
